 "$comment": "OD-1012-LAY-4a regression review. One digest per category|eventType of every observable NotificationRouter decision (Expo messages + delivery-attempt rows) over the routerDecisionMatrix.ts matrix, generated by running that matrix against origin/main 77aac9e50's NotificationRouter.ts + lib/push.ts. routerRegression.test.ts requires the branch to reproduce every digest except the layover return warnings (layover.return.*), which this change re-routes on purpose. Regenerate only from main's sources (see the test header). Regenerated 2026-10-14 (B58 lane LAY-6, census-layover L144) by the same procedure \u2014 77aac9e50's NotificationRouter.ts, lib/push.ts and LayoverReturnEscalation.ts over the branch tree \u2014 when TEMPLATES gained layover.crew.member_heading_back (in-app only). Run on the unchanged tree first, that procedure reproduced all 352 committed digests exactly. A digest covers the decision KEYS, which carry the matrix row index, so every type whose rows are indexed after the appended template re-digests (the 231 synthetic category|eventType types and the four layover.return.* types), while the 117 template types indexed before it keep their digests; the routing itself is unchanged. Regenerated 2026-10-17 (wave 5, census-telegraph T395) by the same procedure, in an isolated copy of the branch tree with 77aac9e50's NotificationRouter.ts, lib/push.ts and LayoverReturnEscalation.ts, when TEMPLATES gained telegraph.coordination (appended last). Run first without that template, the procedure reproduced all 353 committed digests exactly; with it, one type is added (telegraph|telegraph.coordination) and the 235 types indexed after it (231 synthetic + 4 layover.return.*) re-digest for the row-index reason above, while the 118 template types indexed before it keep their digests. The routing itself is unchanged. Regenerated 2026-10-17 (wave 5, lane 7, census-telegraph T256/T397) by the same procedure, in an isolated copy of the branch tree with 77aac9e50's NotificationRouter.ts, lib/push.ts and LayoverReturnEscalation.ts. Run first on the unchanged tree, it reproduced all 354 committed digests exactly. Two template changes: telegraph.message loses the `telegraph` channel (in-app and push only, so a message notification never posts a system message into the thread it reports), and plans|plan.time_confirmed is appended last (the meetup confirm-time notification, through the ledger). Measured separately, the channel change alone re-digests exactly one type (telegraph|telegraph.message). The appended template adds one type and re-digests the 235 types indexed after it (231 synthetic + 4 layover.return.*) for the row-index reason above. The routing code is unchanged. Regenerated 2026-10-17 (wave 5 safety lane, census-telegraph T254/T395/T398) by the same procedure, in an isolated copy of the branch tree with 77aac9e50's NotificationRouter.ts, lib/push.ts and LayoverReturnEscalation.ts. Run first on the unchanged tree (HEAD's TEMPLATES), it reproduced all 355 committed digests exactly. Four templates are appended last: safe_return|telegraph.sos (P0, urgent), safe_return|telegraph.safety_all_clear (P1), location|telegraph.location (P2) and telegraph|telegraph.announcement (P1). That adds four types, and the 235 types indexed after them (231 synthetic + 4 layover.return.*) re-digest for the row-index reason above; no template type indexed before them changed. The routing code is unchanged.",
